Sydney Harry Cohen was born in Baltimore, Maryland on May 7, 1906 to Jewish immigrant parents, Lena (née Dishart) from Russia and Manus (Mannie) from Lithuania.  Both, both spoke English.  His parents had three children that were born 2 years apart, with Syd being the middle child.  Manus left his career as a cigar-maker and opened a grocery store when family moved to Virginia.
The 1910 Census showed the family living close to Lena’s family for two years in the area of Norfolk, Virginia, where his sister Eva was born.   Shortly after that, the Cohens moved to the Mexican border town of El Paso, TX, where Lena and Mannie separated.

